==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Named for the American lawyer and [[horticulturist]] [[w:James Harvey Logan|James Harvey Logan]] (1841-1928).

===Noun===
{{en-noun|loganberries}}

# A [[hybrid]] [[berry]], ''[[Rubus loganobaccus]]'', produced by [[crossing]] a [[raspberry]] with a [[blackberry]].

====Quotations====
*'''2005''' : Brad hesitated, peering at the grid of spun sugar that jutted from his '''loganberry''' parfait. - [[w:Alan Hollinghurst|Alan Hollinghurst]], ''[[w:The Line of Beauty|The Line of Beauty]]'', (Bloomsbury Publishing, paperback edition, 379)

